- agent: agent-a (sub-agent W2A)
- branch: agent/a/m5-w2a-hardening-perf
- task: TASK-079 — perf.New + perf.Manager.RunBaseline implementation
- summary: |
    Implemented perf.New and perf.Manager.RunBaseline per the FROZEN
    JSON Result schema (SchemaVersion=1) pinned in
    rti/internal/perf/baseline.go.

    Harness shape (in-process):
      * Composes federation.Manager + declaration.Manager +
        object.Registry + a multi-federate buffered outbox
        (perfOutbox, bufferSize 8192).
      * Event log INTENTIONALLY OMITTED — both
        federation.Manager and object.Registry accept EventLog: nil
        per cut-1 relaxation. The underlying eventlog.Writer has no
        internal mutex on nextSeq; concurrent senders within one
        federation trip the race detector. The perf harness drives
        exactly that pattern, so it sidesteps the bug. (Documented
        as a non-blocking finding in docs/reports/M5/agent-a.md.)
      * One federation, all federates publish + subscribe to a single
        InteractionClassHandle = 1.
      * Sender goroutine per federate: tight loop on
        objReg.SendInteraction with an 8-byte parameter carrying
        the int64 send-time nanos (encoding/binary, BigEndian).
      * Receiver goroutine per federate: drains the per-federate
        outbox channel, decodes the embedded send-time, samples
        end-to-end latency.
      * Aggregates throughput (sent / wall-clock elapsed) and p50/p99
        latency over the run window. Returns Result with all fields
        populated.

    Constructor New(opts):
      * Validates opts.Size > 0 (returns descriptive error otherwise).
      * Defaults opts.Duration to 10s when zero.
      * Defaults opts.FederationName to "perf-baseline-<size>".

    Result fields populated correctly per spec invariants:
      * SchemaVersion = 1
      * FederationSize = int(opts.Size)
      * DurationSeconds, InteractionsSent, ThroughputPerSecond > 0
      * LatencyP99Ms >= LatencyP50Ms >= 0

    The percentile helper (percentilesMs) handles empty / single-
    sample / 100-sample inputs; covered by TestPercentilesMs.

    Supporting files:
      * rti/internal/perf/outbox.go — perfOutbox (drop-on-overflow
        SubscribableOutbox shape; the cmd/rtid multiOutbox
        crash-on-overflow contract isn't appropriate for sustained
        tight-loop measurement).
      * rti/internal/perf/foms.go — permissive FOMRepository
        (handle-1-resolves-everything; mirrors cmd/rtid's pattern
        without the cmd/rtid import dep).
      * rti/internal/perf/events.go — type alias for the generated
        rtiv1.FederateEvent so extractSendNanos's duck-typed
        Inner() method can resolve.
      * rti/internal/perf/cpu_bench_test.go — build tag `cpuprof`
        helper for re-validating TASK-084's encoding-share
        assumption (used to populate docs/reports/M5/agent-a.md).

- acceptance:
    - go test ./rti/spec/M5/... -run TestSpec_M5_Perf — both 2/2 GREEN.
      (TestSpec_M5_PerfHarnessRuns now passes; the earlier RED-state
      branch is dead code but remains as documentation.)
    - go test -race ./rti/internal/perf/ — race-clean.
    - go test ./rti/internal/perf/ — unit tests pass (NewRejectsZeroSize,
      DefaultsDurationAndFederationName, Size2_ProducesPopulatedResult,
      Size5_ScalesUp, PercentilesMs, JSONShape).
    - go vet ./rti/internal/perf/ — clean.
    - FROZEN JSON schema preserved: snake_case field tags untouched;
      SchemaVersion = 1 unchanged; spec test
      TestSpec_M5_PerfResultSerializesToDocumentedSchema still passes.
